# e2e_manifest.env -- the accounted identity e2e.sh enforces before it trusts a
# board run. Each digest is an md5 of the exact artifact the board loads. Update
# these in lockstep with what is deployed; a mismatch is a fail-closed RESULT
# FAIL, never a silent pass. Override any single entry via the environment.
#
# guest text+data, .hex AND .bin: the flat-exec image the board runs. The
#   servicer/BSCAN path loads the .hex (lnp64_rump_run_dual.tcl); the PS-DAP
#   fastload path loads the .bin (fastload.tcl). Both must be accounted so
#   neither path can boot a stale guest.
# bitstream: the accounted lnp64mini_dual_top.bit -- UNCHANGED across the
#   compiler fix. A new guest does NOT need a new FPGA implementation.
# debug-map: the generated lnp64mini_debug_map.tcl (board_sync keeps the board
#   copy equal to the repo copy).

# Promoted physical-board guest, built with the tp-reserved (fixed) clang.
# Recompiled layer (crt0, librumpuser, md glue, rumpkern threads, shmif/net
# seams, probe) is fixed-clang + native-alloc; reuses the accounted r2 frontier
# cache, exactly the a5b8afb3 recipe with the corrected compiler.
E2E_EXPECT_GUEST_TEXT=866ea6a0f629b3cc7e533631cb3e4e2d
E2E_EXPECT_GUEST_DATA=b2d087fa8d012eafb2024ee54d001bfb
E2E_EXPECT_GUEST_TEXT_BIN=d5d83c680796994a4d3eee51784a2b96
E2E_EXPECT_GUEST_DATA_BIN=bf5dd5bc8e3f271f3da48f8399d895b6

E2E_EXPECT_BIT=e66d2c2221aa6e8dd5df07c55f77c079
E2E_EXPECT_DEBUGMAP=c8994a2af81d368cf4ed60e1c4ef7043

E2E_PING_TARGET=10.106.0.2
E2E_ECHO_TOKEN=e2e-ok-through-gate
